## Files
- `index.html`: GPS collector, runs in the phone's browser (hosted on GitHub Pages)
- `apps-script/Code.gs`: dublinbikes poller, runs on Google Apps Script every minute
- `firestore.rules`: Firestore security rules
- `export.py`: downloads the cloud data to CSV and measures upload delays
- `analyse.py`: Assignment 2 data-quality analysis

## Requirements
Python 3.9+ (tested on 3.14)

## Setup
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate        # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements.txt

## Run

### Collector (own data)
Open https://batutarhan.github.io/gps-tracker/ on the phone, allow location and press start.
Each reading is uploaded to the `gps_fixes` collection in Firestore as soon as it is taken.

### Poller (open data)
Paste `apps-script/Code.gs` into a Google Apps Script project, add the script properties
`FIREBASE_API_KEY`, `FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID`, `POLLER_EMAIL` and `POLLER_PASSWORD`, then run `setup` once.
It writes to `bikes_snapshots`, `bikes_latest` and `bike_stations` every minute.

### Export and analyse
Download a service-account key from Firebase (Project settings > Service accounts > Generate new private key),
save it as `serviceAccount.json` and do not commit it.

python export.py --key serviceAccount.json --out export --hours 24

python analyse.py export/gps_fixes.csv --out figs

`--hours` sets how far back to export. `analyse.py` also still works on a CSV downloaded from the page (`gps.csv`).